  <data name="SequenceAiPrompt" xml:space="preserve"><value>Create one Serial Monitor GUI import JSON object following _manual below. Confirm the actual device protocol, command order, main mode or per-step TxMode (null/Terminal/Hex), line ending (None/Cr/Lf/Crlf or null), post-TX delays in ms, repeat count and existing sequence names. For GUI response checks, also confirm the expected patterns and whole RX Check windows in ms. Reuse supplied information; never invent unknown commands, patterns or checksums. Use FormatVersion:1 for TX-only sequences and FormatVersion:3 if any RX Check exists; change the empty template's version when needed. In v3 set each Kind to Tx or RxCheck. TX puts the real command in CommandText; RX Check requires CommandText to be an empty string and puts its pattern in RxPattern. DelayAfterMs is the post-send delay for TX and the whole check window (0..600000) for RX Check. A match does not end that window early. A check also observes RX received since the preceding TX in the same repeat. RX TxMode:null inherits the preceding enabled TX mode, or the main mode when none precedes it. Terminal patterns are case-sensitive literals with significant whitespace; HEX ?? ignores exactly one byte. Partial nibbles, all-wildcard patterns, regex, subsequence matching, branches, response retries and variables are unsupported. Do not write legacy ResponseCheck or TimeoutMs fields in new files. Sequences without response checks do not collect or save sequence results. For CLI/MCP execution, author a TX-only v1 definition with the requested CaptureMs and optional literal Expect {Kind:text|hex,Value:literal}; those legacy fields do not enable GUI RX Check. CLI/MCP does not support the new RX Check or ?? in HEX expectations. This PascalCase GUI JSON is not the lowercase CLI/MCP save API input. Explicit TxMode preserves command whitespace. A missing literal in interleaved printf does not establish device failure. Use a unique root Name, treat optional step Name/Comment as metadata and include every required field. Preserve _manual and fill empty Steps with the requested real steps. Return only one standard JSON object without comments or Markdown fences, ready to save as UTF-8.</value></data>
